[00:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '[music] Abacus AI Studio just dropped two new features, shorts and aentic avatars. And one of the demos is a 15-second perfume ad, macro shots of light moving through glass, a 360 orbit with speed ramps, [music] liquid'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'breaking in slow motion built from a few product photos, and a paragraph of text. That\'s a six-f figureure spot through a production house normally, and weeks of turnaround. But the output isn\'t the story. What\'s underneath it is because'

[00:27] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A "SHORTS PLAN" UI showing a numbered shot list for a "Virtual Try-On" video featuring "Elodie."
AUDIO: 'every AI video tool up to now has been a slot machine. You write a prompt, you pay, you wait, [music] you find out. Then you tweak a word and do it again. This one researches the actual product'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'first, writes the entire commercial as a numbered shot list, and shows you that list before it renders anything. You read the plan, you approve it, and Cedance 2.5 generates it. An LLM is handling the creative direction, script,'

[00:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'shot sequencing, camera movements pulled from a library of over a thousand cinematic presets. Where the dialogue sits, where the music comes up. The avatars are the other half. Talking head tools have been around for years, but'

[01:08] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A graphic displaying "Seedance 2.5" with a stylized 'S' logo.
AUDIO: 'those were lip-sync bolted onto a static frame with a stock background behind you. What\'s different here is a face that survives a fully generated cinematic scene. The same person walking through Venice, sitting at a cafe,'

[01:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'changing outfits under completely different light across a 30-cond reel. Build the character once and she carries every video after that. We spent a whole video a few days ago pushing Sedance 2.5'

[01:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Inside Higsfield, 30-se secondond scenes, 50 references, multi character consistency, synchronized audio, and that one [music] was about how far the model goes when you\'re the one holding'

[01:46] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A "MULTIMODAL REFERENCING" UI showing various reference images and a video generation preview.
AUDIO: 'the reins. This is the same engine approached from the opposite end of the pipeline. Rendering quality was always going to keep climbing. The more interesting question is what happens when something else decides what to'

[01:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'render in the first place? So, I\'ll skip reexplaining why 32nd generations or native audio matter. What I want to know now is whether a system sitting on top of those capabilities can turn them into'

[02:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'something a creator or a brand could actually use without art directing every single frame themselves. The first demo goes straight at it. Studio gives you three ways into an avatar. There\'s a'

[02:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'built-in library stocked with ready-made personas, a fitness creator, a beauty person, a tech reviewer that kind of spread if you want to start in 10 seconds. You can describe someone in plain English and have Studio conjure a'

[02:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'person who\'s never existed. Or you upload a handful of reference photos and it builds the avatar around a real face, which is the route you take if you want your own likeness carrying content while you never stand in front of a camera'

[02:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'again. Then the voice, and this is where it gets a little uncanny. You can upload a few seconds of a real sample and clone it obviously, but you can also just describe the voice you want and let it synthesize one. The demo spec runs'

[03:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'something like warm, youthful, slightly husky, naturally confident, conversational with a subtle South Asian accent. And out comes a voice matching that description, which you preview with'

[03:13] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Abacus AI Studio UI showing a "Plan accepted — generate the ad" message and "Processing."
AUDIO: 'a test line before you commit. &gt;&gt; Hello there. It\'s lovely to connect with you. I was just thinking about how important it is to find joy in the everyday. Don\'t you agree? From there, you\'re adjusting how the character dresses, how their hair sits, what their'

[03:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'personality reads as, and the whole bundle saves as an identity you own rather than a face that evaporates when the render finishes. The avatar in the demo is called Haley. She goes into the wildcard template. That\'s the open'

[03:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'canvas format. You supply the vision and it produces the film with a genuinely simple brief cinematic luxury travel reel across Italy. Keep her face and skin tone and hairstyle and proportions consistent. Then the agent takes the'

[03:51] [scene:result]
