AUDIO: 'wheel [music] and you can watch it think on the side of the screen. It builds the editorial structure itself, working out where establishing shots belong and at what point Haley should pick up the camera for a handheld selfie moment,'

[04:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'writing what she says when she does. Deciding where the video should breathe and let scenery carry it. Then flowing Rome into Venice into Florence into Lake Ko and out onto the Amalfi coast. different outfits, different hours of'

[04:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the day, completely different light, and the same person holding across all of it while she talks about not having checked her phone in three days, which lands directly on the problem I said was unsolved in that last video. Generating'

[04:28] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Text overlay "Identity persistence" and "Build the person once, reuse that identity in everything afterwards" on a keyboard background.
AUDIO: 'one convincing human is trivial now. Keeping that exact human stable while the wardrobe changes and the sun moves and the camera jumps continents is the wall everybody hits. Abacus attacks it'

[04:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'by promoting the whole thing up a level into a feature they call identity persistence. Build the person once, reuse that identity in everything afterwards. A per project fight becomes a stored [music] asset. It\'s still'

[04:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'generative video underneath. So faces drift and product details break. And notice the demo brief explicitly tells the model not to beautify or reshape the subject between scenes. That\'s a negative prompt. It measurably reduces'

[05:07] [scene:ui]
