AUDIO: 'drift. [music] and you should be stealing it regardless of what tool you\'re in. But even with that caveat sitting there, building a character once and calling her back beats rolling a brand new stranger every time you need a'

[05:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video. Once she exists, she slots into everything studio has. Travel reels, get ready [music] with me, red carpet arrivals, street style, hero transformations, tutorials, [music]'

[05:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'unboxings, reviews, or something completely custom through Wildcard. The templates matter more than they sound like they should because these have proven content structure baked into them. A get ready with me opens'

[05:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'completely differently from an ASMR unboxing. A handheld selfie review needs a rhythm that would kill a cinematic TV spot. A Tik Tok hook has to earn its first 3 seconds in a way a luxury'

[05:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'fragrance film gets to ignore entirely. All that pacing knowledge already lives inside the format and the agent treats it as a production skeleton while writing the actual script and shot plan around whatever you drop in which'

