AUDIO: 'snapping back to his wrist. Several of those apparently needed almost no prompting because [music] Studio picks an avatar personality to fit the product category and writes the rest itself. That\'s the part I keep circling back to.'

[10:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The bottleneck in this whole field is drifting upward. It stopped being about whether the model can render the thing. It\'s about who decides what to render, how it\'s structured, what gets said, what those first three seconds do,'

[11:01] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Abacus AI Studio UI showing a "TV Spot TEMPLATE" with an option to "Add product."
AUDIO: '[music] and what version you try after the first one lands flat. Abacus is automating that layer. And I don\'t see anybody else seriously attempting it yet. The rest of the platform holds it up. Normal image and video generation'

[11:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with access to basically every leading model. Full control over aspect ratio and resolution and duration. Sound on or off. Prompt rewriting if you want a generation optimized before it runs. The'

[11:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'premium avatar path uses Cance 2.5 for clips up to 30 seconds with 2.0 sitting there if you want to spend less and you\'re outputting vertical for Tik Tok and reels or wide for YouTube. You can also crack open any past creation to see'

[11:40] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Abacus AI Studio video editor UI with a historical scene playing, showing "Seedance 2.5" model and generation options.
AUDIO: 'exactly what model and dimensions and duration produced it, then turn it back into a template [music] so the structure becomes reusable. I wouldn\'t come here purely because you want cedence. If you\'re building long cinematic sequences'

[11:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
